<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
  <Content>
    <Paragraph Type="New Act">
      <Text>ACT ONE</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="1">
      <Text>EXT. DINER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DETECTIVE REYES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He's not my brother anymore.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Rain hammers the windows. A neon sign buzzes, dies, buzzes again. She checks her phone. Three missed calls. All the same number. A siren somewhere far off. Neither of them looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text Style="Bold">Headlights</Text>
      <Text> sweep the room. For a second they're both lit up like suspects. Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Headlights sweep the room. For a second they're both lit up like suspects. Rain hammers the windows. A neon sign buzzes, dies, buzzes again. Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="7">
      <Text>INT. PARKING LOT - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAYA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>You said you'd be here at ten. Who else knows?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <ScriptNote ID="1"><Paragraph><Text>Make the diner feel colder.</Text></Paragraph></ScriptNote>
      <Text>She pushes a folded envelope across the table. He doesn't touch it.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat. She pushes a folded envelope across the table. He doesn't touch it. John stares at the coffee like it owes him money.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="12">
      <Text>INT. MAYA'S CAR - CONTINUOUS</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JOHN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I said I'd try. That's not the same thing. You said you'd be here at ten. Who else knows?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DETECTIVE REYES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Tell that to the people looking for him. Sit down. Eat something. We have to talk about the money, and about your brother.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading" Number="17">
      <Text>EXT. POLICE STATION - LOBBY - DAWN</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>A siren somewhere far off. Neither of them looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She checks her phone. Three missed calls. All the same number. He finally opens the envelope. Inside: a photograph, a key, and a ticket stub from the pier.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DETECTIVE REYES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(quietly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He's not my brother anymore.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>John stares at the coffee like it owes him money. He finally opens the envelope. Inside: a photograph, a key, and a ticket stub from the pier.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. PIER - NIGHT</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat. She checks her phone. Three missed calls. All the same number. The waitress drifts past, refills nothing, and keeps going.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Outside, a car door slams. Then another. He finally opens the envelope. Inside: a photograph, a key, and a ticket stub from the pier.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>DETECTIVE REYES</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(quietly)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Sit down. Eat something. We have to talk about the money, and about your brother. I said I'd try. That's not the same thing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She pushes a folded envelope across the table. He doesn't touch it. He finally opens the envelope. Inside: a photograph, a key, and a ticket stub from the pier. Outside, a car door slams. Then another.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JOHN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Parenthetical">
      <Text>(re: the envelope)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>It is tonight. I said I'd try. That's not the same thing.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Transition">
      <Text>CUT TO:</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Scene Heading">
      <Text>INT. MOTEL ROOM - LATER</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>John stares at the coffee like it owes him money. A siren somewhere far off. Neither of them looks up.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat. John stares at the coffee like it owes him money.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>She pushes a folded envelope across the table. He doesn't touch it. John stares at the coffee like it owes him money. Headlights sweep the room. For a second they're both lit up like suspects.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>JOHN (V.O.)</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>I told you not to come back here. Not tonight. Not after what happened at the pier. You never listen. Who else knows?</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>John stares at the coffee like it owes him money.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
