      <Text>MAYA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>He's not my brother anymore. I told you not to come back here. Not tonight. Not after what happened at the pier. You never listen. It is tonight.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Character">
      <Text>MAYA</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Dialogue">
      <Text>Who else knows? I said I'd try. That's not the same thing. You said you'd be here at ten.</Text>
    </Paragraph>
    <Paragraph Type="Action">
      <Text>The waitress drifts past, refills nothing, and keeps going. Maya slides into the booth across from him. She doesn't take off her coat. Headlights sweep the room. For a second they're both lit up like suspects.</Text>
